PATCH 160: the seg-0f69 FILEMGR variant-0 leaf primitives + cluster-dispatch register threading.

The model/KLC/PAL/SKY loads run through the seg-0f69 FILEMGR: 2733 (batch LOAD, DGROUP:0x384), 276e
(streaming OPEN, DGROUP:0x38c), 27e2 (CLOSE, 0x390), 27f7 (READ, 0x394), 280a (SEEK).  Each dispatches
a per-extension-variant leaf handler from the cs:0x2b88.. vtable (base cs=0f69 -> g_mem+0xf690).  For
LOOSE (uncompressed) data files the AH=4300 attr-probe always selects variant0 (the ORIGINAL extension
char; the '!'/'@' packed variants at cs:0x2b7f/0x2b80 are only reached if variant0 is absent), whose
column is the plain-INT-21h leaf set decoded from the image at 0f69:0x2b88:
  LOAD  0x318e = FUN_1000_281e (thunk -> 2593 open+read+close; already recovered)
  OPEN  0x3195 = FUN_1000_2825 (attr-probe+open+lseek-size+seek-0 -> AX=handle; already recovered)
  CLOSE 0x31d7, READ 0x31e1, SEEK 0x31eb  <- the three tiny stubs Ghidra did NOT promote (reached only
                                              through the vtable) -- reconstructed here + fmap-registered.
Route (b) chosen (reconstruct-as-C, keep re_out/fist.c pristine) over re-decompile: only 3 trivial
INT-21h stubs are missing, they call the already-promoted 2593, and re-decompile would NOT fix the
pervasive ES/register base-loss across the model-loader chain (Ghidra drops ES either way) while forcing
a re-thread of 159 patches.

Reconstructed (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin):
- FUN_1000_2867 (0f69:0x31d7): CLOSE -- `cmp bx,1; jb ret; mov ah,0x3e; int 21h` (bx=handle).
- FUN_1000_2871 (0f69:0x31e1): READ  -- `mov ah,0x3f; int 21h` (bx=handle, cx=count, dx=buf, ds=DGROUP).
- FUN_1000_287b (0f69:0x31eb): SEEK  -- `mov ax,0x4200; int 21h` (bx=handle, cx:dx=offset).
Registered at their linear addresses (0x12867/0x12871/0x1287b) in fist_fmap[] so fist_icall_near(0xf69,
off) resolves them instead of trapping to 0.

Cluster-dispatch register threading (the leaves are __allregs = plain-cdecl positional; the args must be
passed at each vtable-dispatch site since fist_icall crosses the register-threading boundary):
- 2733 LOAD dispatch: pass DX=filename (param_2); 281e forwards to 2593, ES(load_seg) via DAT_1000_2b5e
  (published by the caller 19d1, read by 2593 per patch 101).
- 276e + 2688 OPEN dispatch: pass DX=filename (param_2) to 2825.
- 27f7 READ / 280a SEEK: signatures extended to (slot, cx, dx) so the caller-supplied cx=count/dx=buffer
  (offset for SEEK) forward to the READ/SEEK leaf; return AX passed back.

BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows: the whole cluster is reached only on the ACCEPT mission
cascade (4308->18dc->183f->19d1/1a45->2733/276e), which no verify flow drives.  Makes the FILEMGR
primitives REAL/resolvable; the model set actually opening needs the 19d1/1a45/183f ES+filename threading
(the next patch), which feeds these now-consistent cluster methods.
